this is an introduction to the new 3d  printing functionality of version 11 the  main purpose of the 3d printing  functionality is an easy workflow for  immediate 3d printing let's start with  the Triceratops from our 3d geometry  collection and immediately send it for  printing good-news function print out 3d  automatically connects to your local  printer if you do not have a printer or  need higher quality it can upload models  to an online 3d printing service such as  AI materialize the 3d printing workflow  can be summarized in three easy steps  modeling analyzing and printing there  are several different ways to model an  object in version 11 a large volume of  curated 3d printable objects is already  available for example the new property  region returns a geometric 3d printable  object easily import a model from a 3d  repository such as Thingiverse version  11 supports the import and export of 3d  geometry of all standard formats you can  create 3d printable plots with the plot  themes fixed surface and filled surface  the expression below generates a non  printable surface without thickness a 3d  printable solid is created by including  the plot theme fixed surface the  plucking filled surface fills the space  between the surface and a flat base  algorithmically generated you metrics  and 3d printable models start with an  image generate a mesh using image mesh  extrude it with region product for a 3d  printable model analyze models by  returning specific properties let's  start with a space shuttle model compute  its volume find the mass of the model in  aluminum estimate the cost at forty five  cents per surface area check this  of a box needed for shipment 3d printing  does not always work as expected model  flaws such as holes tiny faces and  overlapping faces may occur with CAD or  3d modeling software the unprinted model  collection you have accumulated over the  years may also be faulty version 11  integrates fully automated detection of  mesh defects